Z||000000||85seNUT||12-29-2001||09:02 PM||||it really didnt bother me at first but when i installed my air intake system from west coast fiero it made a LOT of sucking noise that seems to drown out my exhaust.  I am not saying the intake sucks  (hehe) it is friekin awesome and gave me many performance increases, i was just wondering since it is practically sticking out of the car and goes down to the side scoop is there a way to silence it a little bit so its not so distracting.  thanks alot<BR>Adam||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||12-29-2001||10:15 PM||||I imagine you removed the water trap for the air intake, to give you a free flowing system.  The loud sucking sound you hear is the air going in to the engine.  More power = more noise.  One of the prices you pay.<P>I used to like running my old carburated Plymouth with a 4bbl without the air cleaner.  I did sound awsome dumping the 4bbls.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jefrysuko||12-29-2001||10:34 PM||||Anything done to reduce the sound level would probably be a restriction.  I personally don't like the sucking noise so I have always left my intakes as stock.  To each his own...||||reg||1
Z||000003||SLYGUY||12-29-2001||11:41 PM||||I'd never heard an especially loud intake until people started getting silly with their ricermobiles. It sounds more like a weird honking sound (at least on civics). What your car honks a lot now?<BR>I'm all for increasing hp and all, but intake noise would blow (or is that suck?).<BR>Hope you come up with a good way to silence it!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Sly||||reg||1
